  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000141">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A power transformer is a transformer that bears an electrical power transformation function, realized by electromagnetic induction to transform alternating voltage and current systems to different levels at the same frequency for power transmission purposes.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um transformador de potência é um transformador que possui uma função de transformação de energia elétrica, realizada por indução eletromagnética para transformar sistemas de tensão e corrente alternadas para diferentes níveis na mesma frequência para fins de transmissão de energia.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A power transformer is a transformer that bears an electrical power transformation function, realized by electromagnetic induction to transform alternating voltage and current systems to different levels at the same frequency for power transmission purposes.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">power transformer</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">transformador de potência</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000086"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1992"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1991"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000666">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2417"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">temperature sensing process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de sensoriamento de temperatura</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which thermal energy is detected and converted into a measurable signal representing the temperature of a process stream or component.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000449">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b545"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b543"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b532"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b531"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b546"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b544"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b530"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b533"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cooling process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de resfriamento</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which thermal energy is removed from a process stream or equipment component to reduce its temperature in petroleum production equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000273">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um flange é um artefato material caracterizado por uma geometria de aro plano projetante, placa, colar ou nervura, projetado para fornecer conexão mecânica entre componentes.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flange is a material artifact characterized by a projecting flat rim, plate, collar, or rib geometry, designed to provide mechanical connection between components.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flange is a material artifact characterized by a projecting flat rim, plate, collar, or rib geometry, designed to provide mechanical connection between components.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">flange</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flange</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Flange(x) → MaterialArtifact(x) ∧ ∃g(ProjectingFlatRimGeometry(g) ∧ hasCharacteristic(x,g)) ∧ ∃f(MechanicalConnectionFunction(f) ∧ hasFunction(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1052"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every flange is a material artifact that has a projecting flat rim geometry and has the function of mechanically connecting components.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions because this is a constructive type defined by structural geometry. Under OWA, any artifact with projecting flat rim geometry would be forced into the flange category, which could incorrectly classify specialized equipment or complex assemblies that contain flange-like features but serve different primary functions.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1147">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000174"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1918">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasComponentPartAtAllTimes"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000294"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000187">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de medição e transmissão de nível</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">level measurement and transmission function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement and remote transmission of the fluid level within a vessel.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1632"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1631"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b368">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000415"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b699">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000059"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000292">
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every gravity separator is a separator that bears a GravitySeparationFunction</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">separador gravitacional</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gravity separator</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A gravity separator is a separator that performs separation based on differences in specific gravity of the substances being separated.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1353"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(GravitySeparator(x) ↔ Separator(x) ∧ ∃f(GravitySeparationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um separador gravitacional é um separador que realiza separação baseada nas diferenças de gravidade específica das substâncias sendo separadas.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A gravity separator is a separator that performs separation based on differences in specific gravity of the substances being separated.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000102">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma bomba centrífuga é uma bomba que usa força centrífuga gerada por impulsores rotativos com pás para aumentar a pressão do fluido através de uma carcaça voluta.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A centrifugal pump is a pump that uses centrifugal force generated by rotating impellers with vanes to increase fluid pressure through a volute casing.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">centrifugal pump</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">bomba centrífuga</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A centrifugal pump is a pump that uses centrifugal force generated by rotating impellers with vanes to increase fluid pressure through a volute casing.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on physical mechanism. Under Open World Assumption, any equipment with centrifugal impellers and volute casing could be inferred as a standard centrifugal pump, potentially misclassifying specialized hybrid equipment or complex pump systems that contain centrifugal stages but serve different operational roles.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">CENTRIFUGAL PUMP</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b340"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000072"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(CentrifugalPump(x) → Pump(x) ∧ ∃y(CentrifugalImpeller(y) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,y)) ∧ ∃z(VoluteCasing(z) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,z)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every centrifugal pump is a pump that has a centrifugal impeller as component part at all times and has a volute casing as component part at all times.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1914">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000004"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000589">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">phase sequence measurement process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de medição de sequência de fases</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1789"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1788"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which the phase sequence of an alternating-current electrical supply is measured and verified by petroleum production instrumentation.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000675">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2533"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2534"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de suporte e conexão de coluna de produção</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tubing support and connection function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes both the mechanical support of tubing strings within a wellbore and their connection to surface or subsurface equipment.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1449">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000392"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b202">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000026"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000428">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which electrochemical corrosion of a metallic structure is prevented by making it the cathode of an electrochemical cell through the supply of electrical current or sacrificial anodes.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de proteção catódica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cathodic protection process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b316"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b317"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b792">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b793"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b789"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000516">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000466"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1043"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de detecção de chama</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flame detection process</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A detection process in which the presence of a flame or combustion event is sensed by detecting radiant energy or other combustion signatures.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000201">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de proteção de sensor de temperatura</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">temperature sensor protection function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2456"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2455"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2463"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2464"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in a TemperatureSensorProtectionProcess and that consists in providing a protective enclosure for temperature sensing elements while enabling thermal conductivity from the process medium to the sensor.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in a TemperatureSensorProtectionProcess and that consists in providing a protective enclosure for temperature sensing elements while enabling thermal conductivity from the process medium to the sensor.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000363">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">invólucro de transmissor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">transmitter housing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2516"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A transmitter housing is an Assembly that bears an EnclosureFunction and that has a transmitter electronic circuit as a component part at all times, designed to provide environmental protection and physical containment for transmitter components.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um invólucro de transmissor é uma Assembly que possui uma EnclosureFunction e que tem um circuito eletrônico de transmissor como parte componente em todos os momentos, projetado para fornecer proteção ambiental e contenção física para componentes do transmissor.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A transmitter housing is an Assembly that bears an EnclosureFunction and that has a transmitter electronic circuit as a component part at all times, designed to provide environmental protection and physical containment for transmitter components.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">TransmitterHousing ⊑ Assembly ⊓ ∃bearerOf.EnclosureFunction ⊓ ∃hasComponentPartAtAllTimes.TransmitterElectronicCircuit</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(TransmitterHousing(x) → Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(EnclosureFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃c(TransmitterElectronicCircuit(c) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,c)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type based on physical structure as housing. Under OWA, sufficient conditions for transmitter housing would require specifying exact structural features (materials, dimensions, sealing mechanisms) that distinguish it from other instrument housings. The necessary conditions establish the core identity without risking false positives from other housing types that might share some structural features.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2260">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000636"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000230">
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b455"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A compensator is a material artifact that has the designed function of compensating for axial or radial movement between two connected elements.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">compensator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">compensador</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um compensador é um artefato material que tem a função projetada de compensar movimento axial ou radial entre dois elementos conectados.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A compensator is a material artifact that has the designed function of compensating for axial or radial movement between two connected elements.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b459"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A filter is a separator that bears a filtration function to selectively remove unwanted constituents from a fluid stream using a filter element within a filter housing.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b970"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">filtro</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">filter</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um filtro é um separador que possui uma função de filtração para remover seletivamente constituintes indesejados de um fluxo de fluido usando um elemento filtrante dentro de um alojamento de filtro.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A filter is a separator that bears a filtration function to selectively remove unwanted constituents from a fluid stream using a filter element within a filter housing.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Filter(x) ↔ (Separator(x) ∧ ∃f(FiltrationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃e(FilterElement(e) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,e)) ∧ ∃h(FilterHousing(h) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,h))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every filter is a separator that has a filtration function and has a filter element as component part and has a filter housing as component part</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000174">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1141"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1123"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1142"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1122"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1768"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b555"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b554"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1767"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flow measurement function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de medição de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000613">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2048"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2049"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000035"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pressure signal transmission process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de transmissão de sinal de pressão</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A signal transmission process in which a standardised signal representing a measured pressure value is transmitted to a remote control or monitoring system.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000074">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2284"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000092"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2286"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2285"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every shell and tube heat exchanger is a heat exchanger that has a tube bundle as component part and has a shell as component part, where the tube bundle is spatially contained within the shell.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type to avoid false positives under OWA. Any equipment with a shell and tube bundle could theoretically be classified as a standard shell-and-tube heat exchanger, but specialized variants (like graphite shell-and-tube or custom multi-stream designs) should not be automatically forced into this maintenance category without domain expert validation.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">trocador de calor de casco e tubos</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">shell and tube heat exchanger</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A shell and tube heat exchanger is a heat exchanger that has a tube bundle spatially contained within a surrounding shell.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um trocador de calor de casco e tubos é um trocador de calor que possui um feixe de tubos contido espacialmente dentro de um casco envolvente.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A shell and tube heat exchanger is a heat exchanger that has a tube bundle spatially contained within a surrounding shell.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">ShellAndTubeHeatExchanger(x) → HeatExchanger(x) ∧ ∃tb(TubeBundle(tb) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,tb)) ∧ ∃s(Shell(s) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,s) ∧ spatiallyContains(s,tb))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b656">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b654"/>
