  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000237">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">coriolis mass flow meter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">medidor de vazão Coriolis</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b559"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000278"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flow meter that utilizes the Coriolis principle through specialized oscillating flow tubes to directly measure mass flow rate of fluids.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(CoriolisMassFlowMeter(x) → FlowMeter(x) ∧ ∃y(CoriolisFlowTube(y) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,y)) ∧ ∃z(CoriolisPrinciple(z) ∧ utilizesPhysicalPrinciple(x,z)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type. Under the Open World Assumption, defining sufficient conditions based on Coriolis principle usage could lead to false positives where other devices using Coriolis forces (like gyroscopes or accelerometers) might be incorrectly classified as flow meters. The structural differentia provides necessary conditions that can be validated by domain experts.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every coriolis mass flow meter is a flow meter that has component part at all times some Coriolis flow tube and utilizes the Coriolis principle.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flow meter that utilizes the Coriolis principle through specialized oscillating flow tubes to directly measure mass flow rate of fluids.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um medidor de vazão que utiliza o princípio de Coriolis através de tubos de fluxo oscilantes especializados para medir diretamente a vazão mássica de fluidos.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000200">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de interrupção de corrente elétrica</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">electrical current interruption function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b429"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b430"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the interruption of electrical current flow in a circuit under normal operating or fault conditions.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000268">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A filter press is a filter that applies mechanical compression force to enhance the separation of substances through a pressurized filtration process.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(FilterPress(x) → Filter(x) ∧ ∃p(PressureMechanism(p) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p)) ∧ ∃proc(MechanicalCompressionProcess(proc) ∧ participatesIn(x,proc)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma prensa filtrante é um filtro que aplica força de compressão mecânica para melhorar a separação de substâncias através de um processo de filtração pressurizada.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A filter press is a filter that applies mechanical compression force to enhance the separation of substances through a pressurized filtration process.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">filter press</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">prensa filtrante</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1003"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1002"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions because this is classified as 'both' functional and constructive. The structural differentia (pressure mechanism and compression process) involves specific mechanical configurations that are harder to make sufficient under Open World Assumption without detailed engineering specifications.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every filter press is a filter that has a pressure mechanism as part and participates in mechanical compression processes.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1561">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000039"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000239">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">damper</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">amortecedor</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A damper is an assembly that bears the designed function to suppress, regulate, or reduce unfavorable dynamic characteristics such as vibrations, pressure fluctuations, or flow disturbances.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um amortecedor é um conjunto que possui a função projetada de suprimir, regular ou reduzir características dinâmicas desfavoráveis como vibrações, flutuações de pressão ou distúrbios de fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A damper is an assembly that bears the designed function to suppress, regulate, or reduce unfavorable dynamic characteristics such as vibrations, pressure fluctuations, or flow disturbances.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b573"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1410">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000501"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b682">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b684"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000511">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A heating function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the transfer of thermal energy generated by combustion to a process stream or vessel.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1019"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000190"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1020"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de aquecimento a combustão</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fired heating function</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b761">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000472"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1423">
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1421"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000552">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1507"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1506"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de indicação</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">indication process</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which the value of a process variable is measured and displayed locally or transmitted to enable monitoring.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2294">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2296"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1909">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000161"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000420">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b239"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b238"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b240"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b237"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">bottom hole drilling process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de perfuração de fundo de poço</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which subsurface rock at the bottom of a wellbore is cut and disintegrated by a drill bit to advance the drill hole.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b853">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1264">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000571"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000438">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de condensação</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">condensation process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b482"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b484"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b481"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b483"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which a vapour is converted into liquid by removing thermal energy until the substance reaches its dew point in petroleum production equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1494">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000039"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000240">
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every deaerator is a separator that bears a deaeration function for removing dissolved gases from liquids</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deaerator is a separator designed to remove dissolved gases from liquid streams through specialized degassing processes.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">deaerator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">desaerador</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A deaerator is a separator designed to remove dissolved gases from liquid streams through specialized degassing processes.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um desaerador é um separador projetado para remover gases dissolvidos de correntes líquidas através de processos especializados de desgaseificação.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b582"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Deaerator(x) ↔ (Separator(x) ∧ ∃f(DeaerationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1105">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000517"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000190">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1387"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1386"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de aquecimento</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heating function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the transfer of thermal energy to a process stream or vessel to raise its temperature.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000451">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b571"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b572"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">damping function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de amortecimento</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the absorption and dissipation of mechanical energy to reduce the amplitude of oscillations or vibrations.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000169">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the automatic release of process fluid when pressure exceeds a defined set point to protect equipment from overpressure.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2118"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2165"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2166"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2119"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de alívio de pressão</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pressure relief function</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000259">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An eductor is a pump that uses a high-pressure motive fluid jet to create a low-pressure zone that entrains and moves a second fluid via momentum transfer.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um edutor é uma bomba que usa um jato de fluido motriz de alta pressão para criar uma zona de baixa pressão que arrasta e move um segundo fluido via transferência de momento.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000072"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b871"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b872"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An eductor is a pump that uses a high-pressure motive fluid jet to create a low-pressure zone that entrains and moves a second fluid via momentum transfer.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">edutor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">eductor</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Eductor(x) → Pump(x) ∧ ∃n(MotiveFluidNozzle(n) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,n)) ∧ ∃t(VenturaThroat(t) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,t)) ∧ ∃p(JetEntrainmentProcess(p) ∧ participatesIn(x,p)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every eductor is a pump that has a motive fluid nozzle and Ventura throat as component parts and participates in a jet entrainment process.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">The constructive differentia based on jet entrainment mechanism could potentially apply to hybrid or specialized equipment that incorporates eductor principles but should not be automatically classified as a standard eductor type. Under OWA, necessary conditions protect against false positive classifications.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1149">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1147"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b491">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000206">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An accumulator is a vessel that has the designed function to accumulate (store and controllably release) energy or matter.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um acumulador é um vaso que tem a função projetada de acumular (armazenar e liberar de forma controlada) energia ou matéria.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An accumulator is a vessel that has the designed function to accumulate (store and controllably release) energy or matter.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b22"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">acumulador</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">accumulator</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ACCUMULATOR</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Accumulator</skos:altLabel>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (Accumulator(x) ↔ (Vessel(x) ∧ ∃f (AccumulationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every accumulator is a vessel that bears an accumulation function</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b920">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b922"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000179">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b745"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b754"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b755"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000177"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b744"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de medição de pressão diferencial</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">differential pressure measurement function</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PressureSensingFunction that is realized in a DifferentialPressureMeasurementProcess and that consists in sensing the pressure difference between two fluid media or two points in the same medium to enable measurement of differential pressure.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PressureSensingFunction that is realized in a DifferentialPressureMeasurementProcess and that consists in sensing the pressure difference between two fluid media or two points in the same medium to enable measurement of differential pressure.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1353">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1355"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1802">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1551">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000038"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000214">
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every basin is a vessel that bears a storage function and has an open top configuration and is installed partly below grade.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basin is a vessel that is designed to store liquid or solid material, characterized by being typically open at the top and installed partly or totally below grade.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">basin</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">bacia</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b143"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000158"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">Basin(x) ↔ Vessel(x) ∧ ∃f(StorageFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃p(OpenTop(p) ∧ hasGeometricProperty(x,p)) ∧ ∃q(PartlyBelowGrade(q) ∧ hasInstallationProperty(x,q))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A basin is a vessel that is designed to store liquid or solid material, characterized by being typically open at the top and installed partly or totally below grade.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma bacia é um vaso projetado para armazenar material líquido ou sólido, caracterizado por ser tipicamente aberto no topo e instalado parcial ou totalmente abaixo do nível do solo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">BASIN</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Basin</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000123">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000077"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1343"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(GlobeValve(x) → Valve(x) ∧ ∃y,z(hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,y) ∧ LinearMotionClosure(y) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,z) ∧ NormalSeat(z)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A globe valve is a valve characterized by a closure member (disc or plug) that operates with linear motion perpendicular to a seat that is oriented normal to the fluid flow path.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">globe valve</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula globo</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every globe valve is a valve that has as component part at all times a linear motion closure and a normal seat.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula globo é uma válvula caracterizada por um elemento de fechamento (disco ou tampão) que opera com movimento linear perpendicular a uma sede orientada normal ao caminho do fluxo do fluido.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A globe valve is a valve characterized by a closure member (disc or plug) that operates with linear motion perpendicular to a seat that is oriented normal to the fluid flow path.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Using necessary conditions for this constructive type. Under OWA, making the structural differentia sufficient could force classification of specialized equipment containing linear motion closures (like complex multi-way valves or custom manifolds) as standard globe valves when they may warrant distinct maintenance categories.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2142">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1417">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1531">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000110">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A differential pressure transmitter is a pressure transmitter that bears a differential pressure transmission function, enabling it to measure the pressure difference between two input pressure signals and transmit this difference as a standardized output signal.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">transmissor de pressão diferencial</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">differential pressure transmitter</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (DifferentialPressureTransmitter(x) ↔ PressureTransmitter(x) ∧ ∃f (DifferentialPressureTransmissionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A differential pressure transmitter is a pressure transmitter that bears a differential pressure transmission function, enabling it to measure the pressure difference between two input pressure signals and transmit this difference as a standardized output signal.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um transmissor de pressão diferencial é um transmissor de pressão que possui uma função de transmissão de pressão diferencial, permitindo medir a diferença de pressão entre dois sinais de pressão de entrada e transmitir essa diferença como um sinal de saída padronizado.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every differential pressure transmitter is a pressure transmitter that bears a differential pressure transmission function</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b780"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2475">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2477"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000426">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b296"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b295"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de suporte de cabos</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cable support process</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which cables are mechanically supported and routed to maintain their position and protect them from damage in a petroleum production installation.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1578">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2134">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000163"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000445">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b516"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b517"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">control function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de controle</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the regulation of a process variable by adjusting a manipulated variable in response to a measured deviation from a set point.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2125">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2123"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b653">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b655"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000076">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">elemento de temperatura</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">temperature element</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A temperature element is an instrument that bears a temperature sensing function.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um elemento de temperatura é um instrumento que possui uma função de sensoreamento de temperatura.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A temperature element is an instrument that bears a temperature sensing function.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(TemperatureElement(x) ↔ DetectingElement(x) ∧ ∃f(TemperatureSensingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every temperature element is a detecting element that has the function to sense temperature</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2418"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1216">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1217"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000587">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which acoustic energy in a fluid stream or mechanical system is attenuated to reduce radiated noise to an acceptable level.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de silenciamento de ruído</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">noise silencing process</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2300"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2301"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000649">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a stator maintains its fixed position relative to rotating components within machinery, providing structural support and housing for electromagnetic windings, guide vanes, or other functional elements that require stable positioning.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">stationary machine component process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de componente estacionário de máquina</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a stator maintains its fixed position relative to rotating components within machinery, providing structural support and housing for electromagnetic windings, guide vanes, or other functional elements that require stable positioning.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b593">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000456"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b904">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b906"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000256">
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Diverter(x) ↔ MaterialArtifact(x) ∧ ∃f(DivertingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b823"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">diverter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">diverter</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A diverter is a material artifact that bears a designed function to divert or redirect materials, fluids, or flows from their expected course to alternative paths or destinations.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A diverter is a material artifact that bears a designed function to divert or redirect materials, fluids, or flows from their expected course to alternative paths or destinations.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um diverter é um artefato material que possui uma função projetada para desviar ou redirecionar materiais, fluidos ou fluxos de seu curso esperado para caminhos ou destinos alternativos.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every diverter is a material artifact that has the function of diverting materials or flows from expected paths to alternative destinations.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000212">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An anode is electrical equipment that bears the function of serving as the positive electrode in electrochemical processes, capable of emitting positive charge carriers to and/or receiving negative charge carriers from a medium of lower conductivity.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um ânodo é um equipamento elétrico que possui a função de servir como eletrodo positivo em processos eletroquímicos, capaz de emitir portadores de carga positiva para e/ou receber portadores de carga negativa de um meio de menor condutividade.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An anode is electrical equipment that bears the function of serving as the positive electrode in electrochemical processes, capable of emitting positive charge carriers to and/or receiving negative charge carriers from a medium of lower conductivity.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b92"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">ânodo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">anode</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b88"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1812">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000598"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1492">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000689"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000606">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2028"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2029"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de indicação e transmissão de pressão</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pressure indicating and transmission function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement of process pressure and both its local display and the transmission of the corresponding signal to a remote monitoring system.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b294">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000426"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000523">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A FlowControlFunction that is realized in a FlowModificationProcess and that consists in altering the characteristics of fluid flow (such as velocity profile, turbulence, pressure drop pattern, or flow distribution) without primarily controlling the flow rate or direction.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1159"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000026"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1160"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A FlowControlFunction that is realized in a FlowModificationProcess and that consists in altering the characteristics of fluid flow (such as velocity profile, turbulence, pressure drop pattern, or flow distribution) without primarily controlling the flow rate or direction.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de modificação de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flow modification function</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000180">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1416"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1415"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de medição de umidade</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">humidity measurement function</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement and display of the moisture content or relative humidity of a gas stream.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000211">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">angle valve body</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">corpo de válvula angular</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um ValveBody que possui uma geometria de caminho de fluxo interno onde os eixos de entrada e saída são posicionados em ângulo um em relação ao outro, criando uma configuração de fluxo em formato de L ou angular.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A ValveBody that has an internal flow path geometry where the inlet and outlet axes are positioned at an angle to each other, creating an L-shaped or angled flow configuration.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A ValveBody that has an internal flow path geometry where the inlet and outlet axes are positioned at an angle to each other, creating an L-shaped or angled flow configuration.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (AngleValveBody(x) → ValveBody(x) ∧ ∃g (AngularFlowPath(g) ∧ hasGeometry(x,g)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000078"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b84"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type based on geometric configuration. Under OWA, sufficient conditions for geometric characteristics like 'angular flow path' are difficult to specify precisely without detailed geometric constraints that could lead to false classification of complex multi-path valve bodies or hybrid designs.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">AngleValveBody subClassOf ValveBody and hasGeometry some AngularFlowPath</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000352">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A skid is an assembly that bears an equipment support function, consisting of a support frame and mounting points, designed to support equipment items during manufacturing, transportation, handling, and installation.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A skid is an assembly that bears an equipment support function, consisting of a support frame and mounting points, designed to support equipment items during manufacturing, transportation, handling, and installation.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um skid é uma montagem que possui uma função de suporte de equipamento, consistindo de uma estrutura de suporte e pontos de montagem, projetada para suportar itens de equipamento durante fabricação, transporte, manuseio e instalação.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">skid</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">skid</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Skid(x) ↔ (Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(EquipmentSupportFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃s(SupportFrame(s) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,s)) ∧ ∃m(MountingPoint(m) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,m))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every skid is an assembly that bears an equipment support function and has a support frame and mounting points as component parts at all times.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2318"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000326">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A pipeline is an engineered system that bears a fluid transport function, consisting of pipes and possibly including pumps, valves, and control devices, designed for conveying liquids, gases, or finely divided solids between locations.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every pipeline is an engineered system that bears a fluid transport function and has pipe as a component part at some time.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pipeline</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">pipeline</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Pipeline(x) ↔ EngineeredSystem(x) ∧ ∃f(FluidTransportFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um pipeline é um sistema engenheirado que possui uma função de transporte de fluidos, consistindo de tubos e possivelmente incluindo bombas, válvulas e dispositivos de controle, projetado para transportar líquidos, gases ou sólidos finamente divididos entre locais.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A pipeline is an engineered system that bears a fluid transport function, consisting of pipes and possibly including pumps, valves, and control devices, designed for conveying liquids, gases, or finely divided solids between locations.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1893"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000694">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which the flow of fluids from a well is regulated to maintain production targets and prevent uncontrolled release.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b398"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b397"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de controle de fluido de poço</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">well fluid control process</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000365">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A tubing head is a wellhead component that supports the tubing hanger and provides a connection interface for attaching the Christmas tree to the wellhead assembly.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tubing head</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">cabeça de coluna</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A tubing head is a wellhead component that supports the tubing hanger and provides a connection interface for attaching the Christmas tree to the wellhead assembly.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma cabeça de coluna é um componente de cabeça de poço que suporta o suspensor de coluna e fornece uma interface de conexão para fixar a árvore de natal ao conjunto de cabeça de poço.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(TubingHead(x) ↔ WellheadComponent(x) ∧ ∃f(TubingSupportAndConnectionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃p1(TubingBowl(p1) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p1)) ∧ ∃p2(ChristmasTreeConnectionInterface(p2) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p2)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2538"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every tubing head is a wellhead component that bears a tubing support and connection function, has a tubing bowl as component part, and has a Christmas tree connection interface as component part.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
