  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000306">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An input shaft is a shaft that serves as the entrance point for mechanical energy from an external energy source in a power transmission system.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">input shaft</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">eixo de entrada</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1539"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000346"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1540"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um eixo de entrada é um eixo que serve como ponto de entrada para energia mecânica de uma fonte de energia externa em um sistema de transmissão de potência.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An input shaft is a shaft that serves as the entrance point for mechanical energy from an external energy source in a power transmission system.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type based on physical configuration as energy entrance point. Under OWA, defining sufficient conditions could lead to false positives where any shaft receiving external energy input would be classified as a standard input shaft, even specialized or hybrid configurations that should remain in different maintenance categories.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000224">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b335"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000222"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every centrifugal compressor casing is a casing that is intended for use with centrifugal compressors</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A casing that is specifically designed and dimensioned for structural compatibility with centrifugal compressor mechanisms, providing enclosure and protection for rotating impellers and associated flow components.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um invólucro que é especificamente projetado e dimensionado para compatibilidade estrutural com mecanismos de compressor centrífugo, fornecendo contenção e proteção para impulsores rotativos e componentes de fluxo associados.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(CentrifugalCompressorCasing(x) → Casing(x) ∧ ∃y(CentrifugalCompressor(y) ∧ intendedFor(x,y)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">invólucro</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">centrifugal compressor casing</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A casing that is specifically designed and dimensioned for structural compatibility with centrifugal compressor mechanisms, providing enclosure and protection for rotating impellers and associated flow components.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type defined by structural compatibility. Under OWA, asserting equivalence could force classification of any casing with centrifugal compressor compatibility, including hybrid or specialized equipment that should not be automatically classified as standard centrifugal compressor casings.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b936">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000386"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b71">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000173"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000645">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">solid storage and dispensing process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de armazenamento e distribuição de sólidos</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1400"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1399"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which solid materials are stored and dispensed in metered quantities into a process stream.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1065">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000039"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000111">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every double block and bleed valve is a valve that has a primary seat and has a secondary seat and has a bleed port.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula de bloqueio duplo e sangria</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">double block and bleed valve</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (DoubleBlockAndBleedValve(x) → (Valve(x) ∧ ∃p,s,b (PrimarySeat(p) ∧ SecondarySeat(s) ∧ BleedPort(b) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,s) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,b))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A double block and bleed valve is a valve that incorporates two seats each providing sealing capability and includes a means of venting the space between the seats.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula de bloqueio duplo e sangria é uma válvula que incorpora duas sedes, cada uma proporcionando capacidade de vedação, e inclui um meio de ventilação do espaço entre as sedes.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A double block and bleed valve is a valve that incorporates two seats each providing sealing capability and includes a means of venting the space between the seats.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive basis - the structural differentia (dual seats plus bleed port) defines necessary conditions, but under OWA we cannot assert that ANY artifact with these structural components is definitively a double block and bleed valve, as specialized multi-way valves or custom manifolds might contain similar mechanisms without being standard maintenance categories.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000077"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b832"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000315">
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every motor is an assembly that has the function of generating mechanical energy and has as output rotational kinetic energy.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">motor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">motor</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A motor is an assembly that bears a mechanical energy generation function to convert electrical, chemical, pneumatic, or hydraulic energy into rotational mechanical energy.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1735"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A motor is an assembly that bears a mechanical energy generation function to convert electrical, chemical, pneumatic, or hydraulic energy into rotational mechanical energy.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um motor é um conjunto que possui uma função de geração de energia mecânica para converter energia elétrica, química, pneumática ou hidráulica em energia mecânica rotacional.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Motor(x) ↔ Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(MechanicalEnergyGenerationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃e(RotationalKineticEnergy(e) ∧ hasOutput(x,e)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1400">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000040"/>
