  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000100">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A butterfly valve is a valve that has a disc-type closure member with a shaft parallel to the plane of the disc and an axis of rotation transverse to the flow direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">BUTTERFLY VALVE</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Butterfly valve</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Butterfly Valve</skos:altLabel>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A butterfly valve is a valve that has a disc-type closure member with a shaft parallel to the plane of the disc and an axis of rotation transverse to the flow direction.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula borboleta é uma válvula que possui um membro de fechamento tipo disco com haste paralela ao plano do disco e eixo de rotação transversal à direção do fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b283"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000077"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (ButterflyValve(x) → Valve(x) ∧ ∃y(DiscTypeClosure(y) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,y)) ∧ ∃z(TransverseRotationAxis(z) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,z)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">This is a constructive classification based on physical mechanism. Under the Open World Assumption, any artifact with a disc-type closure and transverse rotation axis would be forced into the ButterflyValve class, including specialized hybrid equipment or custom manifolds containing butterfly mechanisms that should not be classified as standard butterfly valves for maintenance purposes.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula borboleta</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">butterfly valve</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every butterfly valve is a valve that has a disc-type closure member and has a transverse rotation axis.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000298">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1439"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000207"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1438"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on hydraulic power source. Under Open World Assumption, asserting equivalence could incorrectly classify complex hydraulic-mechanical hybrid systems or specialized equipment containing hydraulic actuator components as standard hydraulic actuators.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">hydraulic actuator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">atuador hidráulico</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A hydraulic actuator is an actuator that converts hydraulic fluid pressure into mechanical motion through hydraulic power transmission.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um atuador hidráulico é um atuador que converte pressão de fluido hidráulico em movimento mecânico através de transmissão de potência hidráulica.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hydraulic actuator is an actuator that converts hydraulic fluid pressure into mechanical motion through hydraulic power transmission.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b24">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b25"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000158"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b522">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000445"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1529">
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000557"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000303">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An incinerator is a furnace that is designed to combust waste material for disposal purposes.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um incinerador é um forno que é projetado para combustir material de resíduo para fins de descarte.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">incinerador</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">incinerator</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An incinerator is a furnace that is designed to combust waste material for disposal purposes.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Incinerator(x) ↔ Furnace(x) ∧ ∃f(WasteCombustionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every incinerator is a furnace that bears a waste combustion function.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1497"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000218">
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A bottom hole assembly is a drilling component that performs specialized drilling operations at the bottom of the drill string, characterized by including a drill bit and being positioned at the bottom hole location.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um conjunto de fundo de poço é um componente de perfuração que realiza operações especializadas de perfuração na parte inferior da coluna de perfuração, caracterizado por incluir uma broca e estar posicionado no local do fundo do poço.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">bottom hole assembly</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">conjunto de fundo de poço</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b241"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A bottom hole assembly is a drilling component that performs specialized drilling operations at the bottom of the drill string, characterized by including a drill bit and being positioned at the bottom hole location.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000597">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2268"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2269"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pipe shearing process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de corte de tubulação</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which a tubular string within a wellbore is mechanically cut to enable emergency well control.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000075">
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Absorber(x) ↔ (PressureVessel(x) ∧ ∃f(GasAbsorptionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An absorber is a pressure vessel that realizes an absorption function for selective mass transfer of components from a fluid mixture into an absorbent phase.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">absorvedor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">absorber</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b14"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An absorber is a pressure vessel that realizes an absorption function for selective mass transfer of components from a fluid mixture into an absorbent phase.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um absorvedor é um vaso de pressão que realiza uma função de absorção para transferência seletiva de massa de componentes de uma mistura fluida para uma fase absorvente.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every absorber is a pressure vessel that has a gas-absorption function whose realization absorbs specific components from a fluid mixture through mass transfer to an absorbent phase</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b25">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b23"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000131">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A level transmitter is a transmitter that measures the level (height) of liquid or bulk solid material in a container and produces a standardized electrical output signal proportional to the measured level.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">level transmitter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">transmissor de nível</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A level transmitter is a transmitter that measures the level (height) of liquid or bulk solid material in a container and produces a standardized electrical output signal proportional to the measured level.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um transmissor de nível é um transmissor que mede o nível (altura) de material líquido ou sólido a granel em um recipiente e produz um sinal elétrico de saída padronizado proporcional ao nível medido.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1635"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1639"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2654">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/InformationContentEntity"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2304">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/Assembly"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2305"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b201">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2596">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000026"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000320">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">armadilha de pig</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pig trap</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(PigTrap(x) ↔ Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(PigLaunchingAndReceivingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃l(PigLauncher(l) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,l)) ∧ ∃r(PigReceiver(r) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,r)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A pig trap is an assembly that bears the function of launching and receiving pipe pigs for pipeline maintenance and has both launcher and receiver components.</skos:definition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1828"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every pig trap is an assembly that bears a pig launching and receiving function and has component parts that are a pig launcher and a pig receiver.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma armadilha de pig é um conjunto que possui a função de lançar e receber pigs de tubulação para manutenção de dutos e possui componentes de lançador e receptor.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A pig trap is an assembly that bears the function of launching and receiving pipe pigs for pipeline maintenance and has both launcher and receiver components.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b183">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000481"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000683">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de fornecimento ininterrupto de energia</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">uninterrupted power supply process</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which continuous electrical power is provided to critical loads during interruptions to the main power supply.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b441">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000038"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1650">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000601"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b521">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b523"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2341">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2343"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2391">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000161"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000134">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A needle valve is a valve that has a conical needle-shaped closure member that seats into a small orifice to provide precise flow control.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000077"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1746"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma válvula agulha é uma válvula que possui um membro de fechamento cônico em forma de agulha que se assenta em um pequeno orifício para fornecer controle preciso de fluxo.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A needle valve is a valve that has a conical needle-shaped closure member that seats into a small orifice to provide precise flow control.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(NeedleValve(x) → Valve(x) ∧ ∃y(NeedlePlug(y) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,y)) ∧ ∃z(SmallOrificeSeat(z) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,z)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every needle valve is a valve that has a needle plug component and has a small orifice seat component.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">needle valve</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">válvula agulha</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">As a constructive type defined by specific structural features (needle plug geometry), providing sufficient conditions under the Open World Assumption could lead to over-classification. Complex valve assemblies or custom equipment containing needle-like mechanisms might be incorrectly classified as standard needle valves for maintenance purposes.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000260">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">electric actuator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">atuador elétrico</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um atuador elétrico é um atuador que converte energia elétrica em movimento mecânico através de um componente conversor elétrico-mecânico e opera via entrada de sinal elétrico.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">An electric actuator is an actuator that converts electrical energy to mechanical movement through an electric-to-mechanical converter component and operates via electrical signal input.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000207"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b883"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b882"/>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on electrical energy conversion mechanism. Under OWA, asserting equivalence would force any artifact with electrical-to-mechanical conversion into this category, potentially misclassifying specialized hybrid equipment or complex electrical machinery that should not be categorized as standard actuators.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An electric actuator is an actuator that converts electrical energy to mechanical movement through an electric-to-mechanical converter component and operates via electrical signal input.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1485">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000510"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1547">
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1548"/>
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b367">
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000415"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000188">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the measurement and remote transmission of the temperature of a process stream or equipment surface.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">temperature measurement and transmission function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de medição e transmissão de temperatura</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2438"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2439"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000619">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reactive heating function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de aquecimento reativo</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1199"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000190"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1200"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A heating function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the generation and transfer of thermal energy through an exothermic chemical reaction.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000650">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A material artifact that constitutes a pipe made of steel used to convey fluids under pressure in petroleum production piping systems.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">steel pipe</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">tubo de de aço</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2459">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000201"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2147">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000045"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1084">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000396"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2313">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2311"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000266">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A filter cartridge is a filter that has a replaceable filter medium in a cartridge form factor designed for insertion into and removal from a filter housing.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b988"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">cartucho de filtro</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">filter cartridge</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive type where the structural differentia (cartridge geometry and replaceability) is necessary but making it sufficient under OWA could lead to false positives - other equipment containing replaceable filter elements might be incorrectly classified as filter cartridges rather than their proper specialized categories.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A filter cartridge is a filter that has a replaceable filter medium in a cartridge form factor designed for insertion into and removal from a filter housing.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um cartucho de filtro é um filtro que possui um meio filtrante substituível em formato de cartucho projetado para inserção e remoção de um alojamento de filtro.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (FilterCartridge(x) → Filter(x) ∧ ∃m (ReplaceableFilterMedium(m) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,m)) ∧ ∃p (CartridgeGeometryProperty(p) ∧ bearerOf(x,p)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every filter cartridge is a filter that has a replaceable filter medium as component part and bears a cartridge geometry property.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2393">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000493"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1019">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000512"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b823">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b825"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000226">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">corpo de válvula</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">check valve body</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000078"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b366"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A valve body that is specifically designed to accommodate and house the internal mechanisms of a check valve within a pressure-containing boundary.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A valve body that is specifically designed to accommodate and house the internal mechanisms of a check valve within a pressure-containing boundary.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um corpo de válvula que é especificamente projetado para acomodar e alojar os mecanismos internos de uma válvula de retenção dentro de uma barreira de contenção de pressão.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">CheckValveBody subClassOf ValveBody and (designedFor some CheckValve)</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive identity based on structural design for check valve accommodation. Under OWA, any housing designed for check valves could include specialized configurations, custom manifolds, or hybrid designs that should not be automatically classified as standard check valve bodies without domain expert validation of the structural differentia.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(CheckValveBody(x) → ValveBody(x) ∧ ∃y(CheckValve(y) ∧ designedFor(x,y)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1581">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000176"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000653">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">structural support process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de suporte estrutural</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a structural element bears loads, distributes forces, or maintains structural integrity within a system, typically through its geometric configuration and material properties.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A PlannedProcess in which a structural element bears loads, distributes forces, or maintains structural integrity within a system, typically through its geometric configuration and material properties.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b532">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2363">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1536">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1534"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000217">
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x (Boiler(x) ↔ Heater(x) ∧ ∃f(BoilingFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A boiler is a heater that brings a liquid to its boiling point through indirect contact heat exchange, producing steam or vapor.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every boiler is a heater that bears a BoilingFunction and has component parts including a steam drum and heat exchange surface.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A boiler is a heater that brings a liquid to its boiling point through indirect contact heat exchange, producing steam or vapor.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Uma caldeira é um aquecedor que leva um líquido ao seu ponto de ebulição através de troca de calor por contato indireto, produzindo vapor.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b225"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">boiler</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">caldeira</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000196">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">coalescence function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de coalescência</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b438"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b439"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the merging of dispersed liquid droplets into a continuous liquid phase to facilitate their subsequent removal.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2024">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2022"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1815">
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1817"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000652">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de suporte estrutural</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">structural support function</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2466"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2467"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in a StructuralSupportProcess and that consists in providing mechanical support, load distribution, or structural integrity within an engineered system through a flat, planar configuration.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A DesignedFunction that is realized in a StructuralSupportProcess and that consists in providing mechanical support, load distribution, or structural integrity within an engineered system through a flat, planar configuration.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000279">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flow switch is an instrument that bears a flow switching function to automatically open or close electrical circuits when fluid flow rate reaches predetermined threshold values.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">interruptor de fluxo</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flow switch</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flow switch is an instrument that bears a flow switching function to automatically open or close electrical circuits when fluid flow rate reaches predetermined threshold values.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um interruptor de fluxo é um instrumento que possui uma função de comutação de fluxo para automaticamente abrir ou fechar circuitos elétricos quando a taxa de fluxo de fluido atinge valores de limiar predeterminados.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1175"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1171"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000267">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(FilterElement(x) → Filter(x) ∧ ∃m(FilterMedia(m) ∧ madeFrom(x,m)) ∧ ∃a(FilterAssembly(a) ∧ componentPartOf(x,a)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">elemento filtrante</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">filter element</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A Filter that is made from filter media and that is a component part of a filter assembly.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um Filtro que é feito de meio filtrante e que é uma parte componente de um conjunto de filtro.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000081"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b996"/>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">FilterElement SubClassOf Filter and (madeFrom some FilterMedia) and (componentPartOf some FilterAssembly)</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <iof-av:primitiveRationale xml:lang="en">Constructive classification based on material composition (filter media) and mereological relationship (component of assembly). Under OWA, asserting equivalence could lead to unintended classification of any artifact made from filter media as a filter element, including specialized or hybrid components that contain filter media but serve different primary functions.</iof-av:primitiveRationale>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A Filter that is made from filter media and that is a component part of a filter assembly.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</iof-av:isPrimitive>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1761">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasInput"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000045"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000640">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2105"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2104"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A designed function borne by petroleum production equipment whose realization constitutes the reception and re-transmission of a control or monitoring signal to extend its range or provide electrical isolation.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">função de retransmissão de sinal</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">signal relay function</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b698">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000407"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2516">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000500"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000404">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">processo de absorção</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">absorption process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/PlannedProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b10"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b13"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b12"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b11"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A planned process in which one or more gaseous components are transferred from a gas phase into a liquid absorbent phase through contact in petroleum production equipment.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2478">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b2476"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b557">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000037"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000272">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A flame detector is a detector that has the function to detect the presence of flames.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">flame detector</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">detector de chama</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1044"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A flame detector is a detector that has the function to detect the presence of flames.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um detector de chama é um detector que tem a função de detectar a presença de chamas.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b596">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000039"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000253">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A diffuser is an assembly that has the designed function of converting kinetic energy of fluid flow into pressure energy through controlled deceleration in a diverging passage.</skos:definition>
    <iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom xml:lang="en">∀x(Diffuser(x) ↔ Assembly(x) ∧ ∃f(EnergyDiffusionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))</iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">diffuser</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="pt-br">difusor</rdfs:label>
    <iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom xml:lang="en">Every diffuser is an assembly that bears an energy diffusion function and has a diverging channel as component part at all times.</iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b788"/>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="pt-br">Um difusor é um conjunto que tem a função projetada de converter energia cinética do fluxo de fluido em energia de pressão através de desaceleração controlada em uma passagem divergente.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition xml:lang="en">A diffuser is an assembly that has the designed function of converting kinetic energy of fluid flow into pressure energy through controlled deceleration in a diverging passage.</iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b1398">
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000645"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="nb16c18e101c44182af9fd62737a336a6b417">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000431"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054"/>
  </rdf:Description>
